 "teaches": [
  "Name the steps and arrows; the server lays them out (layers, few crossings, right-angled arrows): the call is 1.2 KB of JSON for a diagram hand-placed geometry would spend 15+ KB on",
  "A rejected branch is just an arrow back up (fix > ci): the layout reverses it to keep layers and draws it entering from below",
  "Status per step: ok ticks, active fills, failed crosses, pending mutes; a failed arrow is red. Mono keeps them apart by shape",
  "Top to bottom on a phone, left to right when wide, and Step 4 of 7 with dots when the space is too small"
 ],
